# TSUGI_VERSION check

At the start of a new thread, before other work, compare `TSUGI_VERSION` in `lib/include/setup.php` with the latest local release tag.

Latest means the most recently created tag whose name matches `YY.M.P` (`^[0-9]{2}\.[0-9]{1,2}\.[0-9]+$`). Sort by creatordate, not by version. `29.10.1` is an older mistyped tag and must not win over a newer `26.*` tag.

```bash
git for-each-ref --sort=-creatordate --format='%(refname:lstrip=2)' refs/tags
```

Use `%(refname:lstrip=2)` so a branch with the same name cannot hide the tag.

If they differ, say this once, then continue with the request:

`TSUGI_VERSION of x.y.z is out of date and should be a.b.c`

If they match, or tags cannot be listed, say nothing about the version. Do not edit `setup.php` unless asked.
